            <fragment start="OPS/Kapu_9780375413452_epub_c02_r1.htm#point(/1/2/1/14/1:125)" end="OPS/Kapu_9780375413452_epub_c02_r1.htm#point(/1/2/1/15/1:192)" progress="0.0508475" color="4">
                <text>The European and the African have an entirely different concept of time. In the European worldview, time exists outside man, exists objectively, and has measurable and linear characteristics. </text>
